    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d347">

                <pb facs="0576" n="474" xml:id="pg474"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">550.S1/623: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Atherton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-03-30T16:00:00-05:00">March 30, 1933—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>60. For Davis from Phillips. As of possible interest to you, the British
                    Government has not yet replied to our memorandum, and while several
                    conversations have been held with Lindsay<anchor n="28" xml:id="d347-f1"/>
                    during the past few days they have been exploratory in scope.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d347-f1" n="28" xml:id="d347-f1-content">
                <p>Sir Ronald Lindsay, British Ambassador.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
